# Flutter Best Practices & Coding Standards for MyFamily App

## Core Principles

### 1. NO HARDCODING - EVER
- **NEVER** use hardcoded values for:
  - Dimensions (width, height, padding, margin, font sizes)
  - Colors (use theme colors)
  - Strings (use localization or constants)
  - API endpoints, keys, or configuration
  - Magic numbers
  - Device-specific values

- **ALWAYS** use:
  - `ResponsiveHelper` for all dimensions (w(), h(), sp(), r(), padding(), etc.)
  - Theme colors: `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.*`
  - Constants file for configuration values
  - Environment variables for secrets
  - Localization for user-facing strings

### 2. Responsive Design Philosophy
- **Device-Agnostic**: Code must work on phones, tablets, and desktops
- **Screen Size Adaptation**: Use breakpoints and responsive helpers
- **Orientation Support**: Handle portrait and landscape gracefully
- **Dynamic Layouts**: Use LayoutBuilder, MediaQuery, and responsive widgets
- **Flexible Widgets**: Prefer Expanded, Flexible, ConstrainedBox over fixed sizes

### 3. Architecture & Code Organization
- Follow **Clean Architecture** pattern:
  - `features/` - Feature modules (presentation, domain, data)
  - `core/` - Shared utilities, configs, providers, theme
  - `common/` - Reusable widgets and helpers
  - `data/` - Repositories, models, data sources

- **File Naming**:
  - Use snake_case: `user_profile_page.dart`
  - Suffix pages: `*_page.dart`
  - Suffix widgets: `*_widget.dart`
  - Suffix providers: `*_provider.dart`
  - Suffix models: `*_model.dart`
  - Suffix repositories: `*_repository.dart`

## Code Standards

### Dimensions & Sizing
```dart
// ❌ BAD - Hardcoded
Container(
  width: 100,
  height: 50,
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(16),
  margin: EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 20),
)

// ✅ GOOD - Responsive
Container(
  width: ResponsiveHelper.w(100),
  height: ResponsiveHelper.h(50),
  padding: ResponsiveHelper.padding(all: 16),
  margin: ResponsiveHelper.padding(horizontal: 20),
)

// ✅ BETTER - Use LayoutBuilder for complex layouts
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    final isMobile = ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context);
    return Container(
      width: isMobile ? ResponsiveHelper.w(100) : ResponsiveHelper.w(200),
      padding: ResponsiveHelper.padding(
        all: isMobile ? 16 : 24,
      ),
    );
  },
)
```

### Colors
```dart
// ❌ BAD - Hardcoded colors
Container(color: Colors.red)
Text(style: TextStyle(color: Color(0xFF000000)))

// ✅ GOOD - Theme colors
Container(color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary)
Text(style: TextStyle(color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.onSurface))

// ✅ BETTER - Use theme with opacity
Container(
  color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary.withOpacity(0.1),
)
```

### Typography
```dart
// ❌ BAD - Hardcoded font sizes
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 16))

// ✅ GOOD - Responsive font sizes
Text(
  'Hello',
  style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyLarge?.copyWith(
    fontSize: ResponsiveHelper.sp(16),
  ),
)

// ✅ BETTER - Use theme text styles
Text(
  'Hello',
  style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.titleMedium,
)
```

### Spacing & Layout
```dart
// ❌ BAD - Hardcoded spacing
SizedBox(height: 20)
Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.all(16))

// ✅ GOOD - Responsive spacing
SizedBox(height: ResponsiveHelper.h(20))
Padding(padding: ResponsiveHelper.padding(all: 16))

// ✅ BETTER - Use responsive breakpoints
SizedBox(
  height: ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context)
    ? ResponsiveHelper.h(16)
    : ResponsiveHelper.h(24),
)
```

### Responsive Layouts
```dart
// ✅ ALWAYS use responsive patterns
class ResponsiveLayout extends StatelessWidget {
  final Widget mobile;
  final Widget? tablet;
  final Widget? desktop;

  const ResponsiveLayout({
    required this.mobile,
    this.tablet,
    this.desktop,
  });

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    if (ResponsiveHelper.isDesktop(context) && desktop != null) {
      return desktop!;
    }
    if (ResponsiveHelper.isTablet(context) && tablet != null) {
      return tablet!;
    }
    return mobile;
  }
}

// Usage
ResponsiveLayout(
  mobile: MobileView(),
  tablet: TabletView(),
  desktop: DesktopView(),
)
```

### Grid & List Layouts
```dart
// ✅ Use responsive grid columns
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    final crossAxisCount = ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context)
      ? 2
      : ResponsiveHelper.isTablet(context)
        ? 3
        : 4;
    
    return GridView.builder(
      gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
        crossAxisCount: crossAxisCount,
        childAspectRatio: ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context) ? 0.8 : 1.0,
        crossAxisSpacing: ResponsiveHelper.w(16),
        mainAxisSpacing: ResponsiveHelper.h(16),
      ),
      itemBuilder: (context, index) => ItemWidget(),
    );
  },
)
```

## State Management

### Riverpod Best Practices
```dart
// ✅ Use providers for state
final currentUserProvider = Provider<User?>((ref) {
  final authState = ref.watch(authStateProvider);
  return authState.when(
    data: (state) => state.session?.user,
    loading: () => null,
    error: (_, __) => null,
  );
});

// ✅ Use AsyncValue for async operations
final familyEventsProvider = StreamProvider<List<Event>>((ref) {
  final familyId = ref.watch(currentFamilyProvider)?.id;
  if (familyId == null) return Stream.value([]);
  return ref.watch(eventRepositoryProvider).getFamilyEvents(familyId);
});

// ✅ Handle loading/error states
familyEventsProvider.when(
  data: (events) => EventsList(events: events),
  loading: () => CircularProgressIndicator(),
  error: (error, stack) => ErrorWidget(error: error),
)
```

## Error Handling

```dart
// ✅ ALWAYS handle errors gracefully
try {
  await someAsyncOperation();
} catch (e, stackTrace) {
  // Log error
  logger.e('Operation failed: $e', error: e, stackTrace: stackTrace);
  
  // Show user-friendly message
  if (mounted) {
    ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
      SnackBar(
        content: Text('Operation failed. Please try again.'),
        backgroundColor: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.error,
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Configuration Management

### Constants File
```dart
// ✅ Create constants file for configuration
class AppConstants {
  // API Configuration
  static const String apiBaseUrl = String.fromEnvironment(
    'API_BASE_URL',
    defaultValue: 'https://api.example.com',
  );
  
  // App Configuration
  static const int maxImageSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5MB
  static const List<String> supportedImageFormats = ['jpg', 'jpeg', 'png'];
  
  // UI Configuration
  static const Duration animationDuration = Duration(milliseconds: 300);
  static const Duration snackBarDuration = Duration(seconds: 3);
  
  // Feature Flags
  static const bool enableAnalytics = bool.fromEnvironment(
    'ENABLE_ANALYTICS',
    defaultValue: false,
  );
}
```

### Environment Variables
```dart
// ✅ Use environment variables for secrets
class SupabaseConfig {
  static const String supabaseUrl = String.fromEnvironment(
    'SUPABASE_URL',
    defaultValue: '',
  );
  
  static const String supabaseAnonKey = String.fromEnvironment(
    'SUPABASE_ANON_KEY',
    defaultValue: '',
  );
}
```

## Widget Best Practices

### Reusable Widgets
```dart
// ✅ Create reusable, responsive widgets
class ResponsiveCard extends StatelessWidget {
  final Widget child;
  final EdgeInsets? padding;
  final EdgeInsets? margin;

  const ResponsiveCard({
    required this.child,
    this.padding,
    this.margin,
  });

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final isMobile = ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context);
    
    return Card(
      margin: margin ?? ResponsiveHelper.padding(
        all: isMobile ? 8 : 16,
      ),
      child: Padding(
        padding: padding ?? ResponsiveHelper.padding(
          all: isMobile ? 16 : 24,
        ),
        child: child,
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

### Conditional Rendering
```dart
// ✅ Use conditional rendering based on device
if (ResponsiveHelper.isTablet(context))
  TabletLayout()
else
  MobileLayout()

// ✅ Or use LayoutBuilder
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    if (constraints.maxWidth > ResponsiveHelper.tabletBreakpoint) {
      return DesktopLayout();
    } else if (constraints.maxWidth > ResponsiveHelper.mobileBreakpoint) {
      return TabletLayout();
    } else {
      return MobileLayout();
    }
  },
)
```

## Navigation

```dart
// ✅ Use go_router for navigation
context.go('/profile');
context.push('/profile/edit');
context.pop();

// ✅ Never hardcode routes
// ❌ BAD: context.go('/profile')
// ✅ GOOD: context.go(AppRoutes.profile)
```

## Accessibility

```dart
// ✅ ALWAYS add accessibility labels
IconButton(
  icon: Icon(Icons.delete),
  onPressed: () {},
  tooltip: 'Delete item',
)

Semantics(
  label: 'User profile picture',
  child: CircleAvatar(...),
)

// ✅ Use semantic labels
TextButton(
  onPressed: () {},
  child: Text('Save'),
  semanticsLabel: 'Save changes',
)
```

## Performance

```dart
// ✅ Use const constructors where possible
const SizedBox(height: 16)
const Icon(Icons.home)

// ✅ Use ListView.builder for long lists
ListView.builder(
  itemCount: items.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => ItemWidget(item: items[index]),
)

// ✅ Use keys for stateful widgets in lists
ListView.builder(
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => ItemWidget(
    key: ValueKey(items[index].id),
    item: items[index],
  ),
)
```

