## Code Review Checklist

Before submitting code, ensure:
- [ ] No hardcoded dimensions, colors, or strings
- [ ] All UI uses ResponsiveHelper
- [ ] All colors use Theme
- [ ] Layouts adapt to different screen sizes
- [ ] Error handling is implemented
- [ ] Loading states are shown
- [ ] Accessibility labels are added
- [ ] Code follows clean architecture
- [ ] Widgets are reusable and testable
- [ ] No magic numbers
- [ ] Configuration values are in constants
- [ ] Secrets are in environment variables

## Examples of What NOT to Do

```dart
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS:

// Hardcoded dimensions
Container(width: 100, height: 50)

// Hardcoded colors
Container(color: Colors.blue)
Text(style: TextStyle(color: Color(0xFF000000)))

// Hardcoded strings (unless in constants)
Text('Welcome to MyFamily')

// Hardcoded API endpoints
final response = await http.get('https://api.example.com/users');

// Magic numbers
if (value > 100) { ... }

// Device-specific code without checks
if (Platform.isIOS) {
  // iOS-specific code
}
```

## Examples of What TO Do

```dart
// ✅ ALWAYS DO THIS:

// Responsive dimensions
Container(
  width: ResponsiveHelper.w(100),
  height: ResponsiveHelper.h(50),
)

// Theme colors
Container(
  color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary,
)

// Localized or constant strings
Text(AppStrings.welcomeMessage)

// Configuration-based API calls
final response = await http.get('${AppConstants.apiBaseUrl}/users');

// Named constants
if (value > AppConstants.maxValue) { ... }

// Platform checks with fallbacks
if (Platform.isIOS) {
  // iOS-specific code
} else {
  // Fallback code
}
```

## Responsive Design Patterns

### Breakpoint-Based Layouts
```dart
// ✅ Use breakpoints for layout changes
Widget buildLayout(BuildContext context) {
  final width = MediaQuery.of(context).size.width;
  
  if (width > ResponsiveHelper.tabletBreakpoint) {
    return DesktopLayout();
  } else if (width > ResponsiveHelper.mobileBreakpoint) {
    return TabletLayout();
  } else {
    return MobileLayout();
  }
}
```

### Flexible Grids
```dart
// ✅ Responsive grid columns
int getGridColumns(BuildContext context) {
  if (ResponsiveHelper.isDesktop(context)) return 4;
  if (ResponsiveHelper.isTablet(context)) return 3;
  return 2;
}
```

### Adaptive Padding
```dart
// ✅ Responsive padding
EdgeInsets getAdaptivePadding(BuildContext context) {
  return ResponsiveHelper.padding(
    all: ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context) ? 16 : 24,
    horizontal: ResponsiveHelper.isMobile(context) ? 16 : 32,
  );
}
```

## Summary

**Remember:**
1. **NO HARDCODING** - Use ResponsiveHelper, Theme, Constants
2. **RESPONSIVE FIRST** - Design for all screen sizes
3. **CLEAN ARCHITECTURE** - Follow feature-based structure
4. **ERROR HANDLING** - Always handle errors gracefully
5. **ACCESSIBILITY** - Add semantic labels
6. **PERFORMANCE** - Use const, ListView.builder, keys
7. **TESTABILITY** - Make widgets testable
8. **CONFIGURATION** - Use constants and environment variables

**Every line of code should be:**
- Responsive
- Theme-aware
- Device-agnostic
- Maintainable
- Testable
- Accessible

